it's possible to be an ethical consumer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:23.160
today's globalized society?
Speaker 1: Yeah. You know, I've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:28.740
got you. It wasn't you who called with this exact&nbsp;
same question, like, a month ago, right? No, no,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:35.640
it was okay. Yeah. So. Okay, here's. Here's the&nbsp;
thing. Let's assume the answer is no. You can't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:40.140
be an ethical consumer in this society then.&nbsp;
Then what do we do? What's what do we do based&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:43.680
on that? If that were the answer, just indulge&nbsp;
me for a moment. Let's say I said, you know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:48.900
yo, yo, Al, you can't be an ethical consumer&nbsp;
right now. Nope. What would what would you do?&nbsp;

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:55.320
