companies that still exploit workers and in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:25.020
China and in Bangladesh and whatnot. Right.&nbsp;
So it almost seems like no matter what I do.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:29.820
I mean, I'm in. I'm just being a&nbsp;
hypocrite. You know? Yeah. I'm choosing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:33.600
what I think is personally important to me.
Speaker 1: I know exactly what you're saying.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:41.160
This is the difficulty. And we've we need to find&nbsp;
the balance between living completely off the grid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:46.380
and isolating yourself from all of these things,&nbsp;
which almost none of us are willing to do. I mean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:55.500
almost literally, no one is willing to do that&nbsp;
or doing the best we can to both make decisions.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.500 --> 00:02:01.020
We feel okay doesn't we don't have to feel great,&nbsp;
but we feel like we can accept the decisions we're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:10.320
making and where we think things are not right.&nbsp;
Doing what we can as activists to effect change.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:15.840
So at the end of the day, I mean, you make a good&nbsp;
point. I covered for a decade leading up to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:22.860
